--
--   Slab{ ... }  Stairs{ ... }  Fence{ ... }  FenceGate{ ... }  Door{ ... }
--     exactly the same lines as Block{ ... } (Name, Tab, Color, Texture ...) - you just get that SHAPE with your textures.
--     Optional  Base = "Oak Planks"  adds crafting recipes (slab, stairs, fence, gate) made from that block.
--     Door{...} can have TWO pictures: DoorTop = "id" (top half of the door) and DoorBottom = "id" (bottom half). (Texture = {FrontTop = , FrontBottom = } works too)
--
--   Face shortcuts inside Texture (explicit faces always win):
--     All       = one image for all 6 faces      (or  Texture = "rbxassetid://...")
--     Side      = Left + Right + Front + Back
--     TopBottom = Top + Bottom                   (also called Ends)
--   An empty "" face just uses the block's Color.
--
--   Block options:
--     Pillar = true   -> like a log: the top points the way you placed it
--     (normal blocks never turn - they always sit the same way)
--     Facing = true   -> like a furnace / chest: the Front face looks back at you when you place it
--     Tint = C(r,g,b) -> colors the textures (used for the colored wool)
--     Material, Transparency, Stack
--
--   Item{ Name = "", Tab = "", Front = "rbxassetid://..." }   for tools / food
--     (only the Front image is used). Food = hunger points, Stack = max stack.
--
--   Tab must be one of the names in TOP_TABS / BOTTOM_TABS below.
--   (everything also shows up in the "Search Items" tab)
--====================================================================
